<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Splunk Spend Audit</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #ffffff; --fg: #1a1a1a; --muted: #5f6b7a; --border: #e2e6ea;
    --accent: #0b5fff; --waste: #b3261e; --review: #b06d00; --high: #1a7f37;
    --protected: #6e5aa6; --unknown: #5f6b7a; --normal: #3a4750;
  }
  body { font-family: -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
         color: var(--fg); background: var(--bg); max-width: 960px; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1.5rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 0.2rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin-top: 2.2rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); padding-bottom: 0.3rem; }
  .subtitle { color: var(--muted); margin-top: 0; }
  .summary-box { background: #f6f8fa; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem 1.2rem; margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem; }
  .summary-box p { margin: 0.3rem 0; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 0.8rem 0 1.4rem; font-size: 0.92rem; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 0.4rem 0.6rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  th { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; }
  tr:hover { background: #fafbfc; }
  .badge { display: inline-block; padding: 0.1rem 0.5rem; border-radius: 999px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 600; color: #fff; }
  .badge-POSSIBLE_WASTE { background: var(--waste); }
  .badge-REVIEW { background: var(--review); }
  .badge-HIGH_VALUE { background: var(--high); }
  .badge-PROTECTED { background: var(--protected); }
  .badge-UNKNOWN { background: var(--unknown); }
  .badge-NORMAL { background: var(--normal); }
  .candidate-card { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
  .candidate-card h3 { margin: 0 0 0.3rem; font-size: 1rem; }
  .candidate-meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.88rem; margin: 0.3rem 0; }
  .candidate-explanation { margin: 0.5rem 0; }
  .candidate-recommendation { font-weight: 600; }
  .risk-box, .methodology-box { background: #fff8ec; border: 1px solid #f1d9a0; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem 1.2rem; font-size: 0.92rem; }
  .methodology-box { background: #f6f8fa; border-color: var(--border); }
  .reduced-confidence-notice { background: #fff3f0; border: 1px solid #f0b8a8; border-radius: 6px; padding: 0.6rem 0.9rem; }
  .footer-note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.82rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
  code { background: #f0f2f5; padding: 0.1rem 0.3rem; border-radius: 4px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<h1>Splunk Spend Audit</h1>
<p class="subtitle">Generated {{ generated_at }} — Log Spend Auditor v{{ tool_version }}</p>

<h2>Executive Summary</h2>
<div class="summary-box">
  <p>Your Splunk environment ingests <strong>{{ current_ingest_display }}/day</strong>
     across {{ total_datasets }} (index, sourcetype) datasets.</p>
  <p>Of that, <strong>{{ savings_display.candidate_gb_day }}/day</strong>
     ({{ (savings.potential_reduction_pct * 100) | round(1) }}%) are flagged as
     optimization candidates with low or no observed usage.</p>
  {% if savings.potential_annual_saving is not none %}
  <p>Based on
     {% if savings.annual_spend_input is not none %}
     an annual Splunk spend of <strong>${{ "{:,.0f}".format(savings.annual_spend_input) }}</strong>
     <em>(as provided for this audit, not measured or inferred by this tool)</em>,
     {% else %}
     the cost-per-GB/day you provided,
     {% endif %}
     this represents a <strong>potential annual saving of around
     ${{ "{:,.0f}".format(savings.potential_annual_saving) }}</strong>.</p>
  {% endif %}
  <p><em>This is a potential saving, not a guaranteed one — see "Risk Considerations" below.</em></p>
  <p class="candidate-meta">{{ counts_summary_line }}</p>
</div>

<h2>Current Environment</h2>
<table>
  {% if source_label %}<tr><th>Data source</th><td>{{ source_label }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
  <tr><th>Audit generated</th><td>{{ generated_at }}</td></tr>
  <tr><th>Lookback window</th><td>{{ lookback_days }} days</td></tr>
  <tr><th>Signals available</th><td>{{ available_signal_count }} of {{ applicable_signal_count }} applicable to this run</td></tr>
  {% if reduced_confidence %}
  <tr><th>Signals degraded</th><td>{{ degraded_signal_names | join(", ") }} — see Methodology</td></tr>
  {% endif %}
  {% if has_not_applicable_signals %}
  <tr><th>Signals not applicable</th><td>{{ not_applicable_signal_names | join(", ") }} — see Methodology</td></tr>
  {% endif %}
</table>

<h2>Current Spend</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Current ingest</th><td>{{ current_ingest_display }}/day</td></tr>
  {% if savings.annual_spend_input is not none %}
  <tr><th>Annual Splunk spend used for this estimate</th><td>${{ "{:,.0f}".format(savings.annual_spend_input) }} <em>(user-provided input, not measured by this tool)</em></td></tr>
  {% elif savings.cost_per_gb_day_input is not none %}
  <tr><th>Cost per GB/day used for this estimate</th><td>${{ savings.cost_per_gb_day_input }} <em>(user-provided input)</em></td></tr>
  {% else %}
  <tr><th>Spend estimate</th><td>Not provided — showing volume/percentage only</td></tr>
  {% endif %}
  <tr><th>High-ingest threshold (this environment, p75)</th><td>{{ high_ingest_threshold_display }}/day</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>Ingestion Breakdown</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Dataset</th><th>Volume/day</th><th>% of total</th></tr>
  {% for row in ingestion_breakdown %}
  <tr><td><code>{{ row.name }}</code></td><td>{{ row.gb_per_day_display }}</td><td>{{ row.pct_of_total }}%</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
{% if ingestion_breakdown_truncated %}
<p class="footer-note">Showing top {{ ingestion_breakdown | length }} of {{ total_datasets }} datasets.
{% if tier == "free" %}Upgrade to the full report to see all datasets.{% endif %}</p>
{% endif %}

{% if usage_analysis %}
<h2>Usage Analysis</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Dataset</th><th>Searches 30d</th><th>Searches 90d</th><th>Scheduled</th><th>Alert</th><th>Dashboard</th><th>Users 30d</th><th>Last data observed (days)</th><th>Search evidence confidence</th></tr>
  {% for row in usage_analysis %}
  <tr>
    <td><code>{{ row.name }}</code></td>
    <td>{{ row.searches_30d }}</td>
    <td>{{ row.searches_90d }}</td>
    <td>{{ "Yes" if row.is_scheduled else "No" }}</td>
    <td>{{ "Yes" if row.has_alert else "No" }}</td>
    <td>{{ row.dashboards_display }}</td>
    <td>{{ row.unique_users_30d }}</td>
    <td>{{ row.last_seen_days_ago if row.last_seen_days_ago is not none else "—" }}</td>
    <td>{{ row.confidence }}</td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
{% endif %}

<h2>Top Optimization Candidates</h2>
{% if top_candidates %}
  {% for c in top_candidates %}
  <div class="candidate-card">
    <h3><code>{{ c.name }}</code> <span class="badge badge-{{ c.classification }}">{{ c.classification }}</span></h3>
    <p class="candidate-meta">
      Ingest: {{ c.gb_per_day_display }}/day ·
      Searches 30d: {{ c.searches_30d }} ·
      Searches 90d: {{ c.searches_90d }} ·
      Scheduled: {{ "Yes" if c.is_scheduled else "No" }} ·
      Alerts: {{ "Yes" if c.has_alert else "No" }} ·
      Dashboards: {{ c.dashboards_display }}
      {% if c.last_seen_days_ago is not none %} · Last data observed: {{ c.last_seen_days_ago }} days ago{% endif %}
    </p>
    <p class="candidate-explanation">{{ c.explanation }}</p>
    <p class="candidate-recommendation">Recommendation: {{ c.recommendation }}</p>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
  {% if candidates_truncated %}
  <p class="footer-note">Showing top {{ top_candidates | length }} candidates.
     {% if tier == "free" %}Upgrade to the full report to see all candidates.{% endif %}</p>
  {% endif %}
{% else %}
  <p>No optimization candidates were found with the current thresholds.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>Protected / High Value</h2>
{% if recognized_datasets %}
<p>Not every dataset is a candidate for review — the engine also recognizes
   data it should <strong>never</strong> touch and data it found real evidence
   of active use for. Showing {{ recognized_datasets | length }} of
   {{ protected_count + high_value_count }} ({{ protected_count }} protected,
   {{ high_value_count }} high value).</p>
<table>
  <tr><th>Dataset</th><th>Volume/day</th><th>Classification</th><th>Why</th></tr>
  {% for row in recognized_datasets %}
  <tr>
    <td><code>{{ row.name }}</code></td>
    <td>{{ row.gb_per_day_display }}</td>
    <td><span class="badge badge-{{ row.classification }}">{{ row.classification }}</span></td>
    <td>{{ row.reason }}</td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
{% if recognized_truncated %}
<p class="footer-note">Showing {{ recognized_datasets | length }} of {{ protected_count + high_value_count }} — see full detail below.</p>
{% endif %}
{% else %}
<p>No datasets were classified as protected or high value in this run.</p>
{% endif %}

{% if all_datasets_detail %}
<h2>Indexes / Sourcetypes (full detail)</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Dataset</th><th>Volume/day</th><th>Classification</th><th>Data Value Score</th></tr>
  {% for row in all_datasets_detail %}
  <tr>
    <td><code>{{ row.name }}</code></td>
    <td>{{ row.gb_per_day_display }}</td>
    <td><span class="badge badge-{{ row.classification }}">{{ row.classification }}</span></td>
    <td>{{ row.score }}</td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
{% endif %}

<h2>Potential Savings</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Current ingest</th><td>{{ savings_display.current_ingest_gb_day }}/day</td></tr>
  <tr><th>Possible waste</th><td>{{ savings_display.possible_waste_gb_day }}/day</td></tr>
  <tr><th>Review candidates (weighted ×{{ review_weight }})</th><td>{{ savings_display.review_gb_day }}/day</td></tr>
  <tr><th>Total optimization candidate volume</th><td>{{ savings_display.candidate_gb_day }}/day</td></tr>
  <tr><th>Potential reduction</th><td>{{ (savings.potential_reduction_pct * 100) | round(1) }}%</td></tr>
  {% if savings.potential_annual_saving is not none %}
  <tr><th>Potential annual saving</th><td>${{ "{:,.0f}".format(savings.potential_annual_saving) }}</td></tr>
  {% endif %}
</table>
<p class="footer-note">This is a potential saving estimate, not a promise of
   savings — see the assumptions in "Methodology" below.</p>

<h2>Risk Considerations</h2>
<div class="risk-box">
  <p>This tool is <strong>read-only</strong>: it never modifies, deletes, or
     disables anything in Splunk. It only reads metadata (ingest volume and
     usage signals) — see docs/security.md.</p>
  <p>These figures are estimates based on Splunk metadata (ingest volume and
     search/alert/dashboard activity), <strong>not a financial audit</strong>.</p>
  <p>Datasets classified as <span class="badge badge-PROTECTED">PROTECTED</span>
     were deliberately excluded from optimization candidates, regardless of
     their usage signals.</p>
  <p>Datasets classified as <span class="badge badge-UNKNOWN">UNKNOWN</span>
     are excluded from the savings calculation — we could not determine
     their usage with high confidence, so we do not guess.</p>
  {% if show_squashing_note %}
  <p>This report analyzes usage at the (index, sourcetype) level only. Splunk's
     license usage reporting can "squash" host and source breakdowns in
     high-cardinality environments — see Methodology.</p>
  {% endif %}
  <p><strong>No action should be taken without manual validation by a Splunk
     administrator and the team that owns each dataset.</strong></p>
</div>

<h2>Recommendations</h2>
<ul>
{% for r in recommendations %}
  <li>{{ r }}</li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>

<h2>Methodology</h2>
<div class="methodology-box">
  <p>Lookback window: {{ lookback_days }} days. Unit of analysis: (index, sourcetype)
     — see Risk Considerations for why host/source are not used as a
     classification basis.</p>
  <p>Search-evidence coverage: {{ ((1 - partial_or_unknown_ratio) * 100) | round(1) }}%
     of analyzed searches were parsed with high confidence
     ({{ (partial_or_unknown_ratio * 100) | round(1) }}% were partial/unknown
     and excluded from waste classification — see docs/scoring.md).</p>
  {% if reduced_confidence %}
  <p class="reduced-confidence-notice"><strong>Analysis completed with reduced confidence.</strong>
     Unavailable signals: {{ degraded_signal_names | join(", ") }}. A dataset
     is never classified as a waste candidate based on a signal from an
     unavailable source — see docs/architecture.md.</p>
  {% endif %}
  <p>Data sources available in this run:</p>
  <ul>
  {% for row in sources_available_display %}
    <li><code>{{ row.source }}</code>: {{ row.label }}</li>
  {% endfor %}
  </ul>
  <p>Generated by Log Spend Auditor v{{ tool_version }} on {{ generated_at }}.</p>
</div>

</body>
</html>
